                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f7ec5f89-3211-47b7-91d7-af2bd76bad63",
                        "source_entry_id": "67006890-7ead-30f1-bd9c-add630a5346c",
                        "source_sense_id": "5f6c20d7-ee34-3163-bc90-5c6f525af2cf",
                        "target_lang_word": "fugue",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fugue",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "646df55e-cdda-3bef-9673-977fb80597c7",
                                        "entry_id": "9314b7b0-2305-3163-8d83-6d05ee8ef50c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A contrapuntal piece of music wherein a particular melody is played in a number of voices, each voice introduced in turn by playing the melody."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1af70b0b-c316-384d-9cde-42b045e11dd2",
                                        "entry_id": "9314b7b0-2305-3163-8d83-6d05ee8ef50c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anything in literature, poetry, film, painting, etc., that resembles a fugue in structure or in its elaborate complexity and formality."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "746ee821-b41b-4ecc-977f-7d17d119fe53",
                                                "sense_id": "1af70b0b-c316-384d-9cde-42b045e11dd2",
                                                "text": "Jacobsen's theory about the empty storehouse is still valid, for a myth never has one meaning only; a myth is a polyphonic fugue of many voices."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4f0f0b85-e6aa-31cd-b2d0-224c4dbd4e2a",
                                        "entry_id": "9314b7b0-2305-3163-8d83-6d05ee8ef50c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fugue state."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "fugue",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b58a8718-de46-39b8-8716-354dbb74a413",
                                        "entry_id": "aaf68a4b-6953-378e-b95a-aebfd223e45b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To improvise, in singing, by introducing vocal ornamentation to fill gaps etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a480539c-0164-3352-a8f7-5067bbe6bc96",
                                        "entry_id": "aaf68a4b-6953-378e-b95a-aebfd223e45b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To spend time in a dissociative fugue state."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6cf9a7e1-7ab3-4be5-831c-adfd1778a6e2",
                                                "sense_id": "a480539c-0164-3352-a8f7-5067bbe6bc96",
                                                "text": "And most of them women, and these only stayed in a fugue state for a relatively short time, like a couple of hours or a couple of days. As far as we know Malenov fugued for close to twenty years."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f6cdb356-7052-48f5-aba9-db316d2ee7ec",
                                                "sense_id": "a480539c-0164-3352-a8f7-5067bbe6bc96",
                                                "text": "Fugue states can have phases—it's possible she fugued from the start, and only woke to what was happening on that bus."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "47f5eac0-a313-41e2-85ca-b96172f5b526",
                        "source_entry_id": "67006890-7ead-30f1-bd9c-add630a5346c",
                        "source_sense_id": "5f6c20d7-ee34-3163-bc90-5c6f525af2cf",
                        "target_lang_word": "fugue",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fugue",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8a25d99a-28bd-3d61-ba32-0db2d8609dc1",
                                        "entry_id": "15c663d3-e09c-3127-aa96-0b9d5b79876d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fuite."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85e2a512-a1ce-42aa-9ae0-d7f9fc6031ea",
                                                "sense_id": "8a25d99a-28bd-3d61-ba32-0db2d8609dc1",
                                                "text": "Vous dites que vous méditez une fugue dans mes déserts, et vous me proposez de quitter mes déserts pour le fracas de Paris !"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f3ac956-9725-4c26-87a5-35f0be6e9a4e",
                                                "sense_id": "8a25d99a-28bd-3d61-ba32-0db2d8609dc1",
                                                "text": "On avait beau le corriger quand les voisins le ramenait en carriole, l'habitude de ces fugues était prise. […]. Si une semaine s'écoulait sans escapade, on le voyait s'ennuyer, dépérir et fureter dans le logis pour trouver une issue."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8ae988be-42fe-30a4-a474-ec7e974a18fb",
                                        "entry_id": "15c663d3-e09c-3127-aa96-0b9d5b79876d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Morceau de musique, ou passage d’un morceau de musique, dans lequel différentes parties se suivent, se succèdent et semblent fuir et se poursuivre tour à tour, en répétant le même sujet d’après des règles établies. On parle de sujet, contre-sujet, réponse, exposition, épisodes, reprises modulées, stretto et pédales."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd87eb2f-0817-4ed8-9f63-f0a1dbec6d15",
                                                "sense_id": "8ae988be-42fe-30a4-a474-ec7e974a18fb",
                                                "text": "Lully fut le premier en France qui fit des basses, des milieux et des fugues."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88400d07-d3f5-4039-bc19-3db73bb0ea7c",
                                                "sense_id": "8ae988be-42fe-30a4-a474-ec7e974a18fb",
                                                "text": "La fugue est l’ingrat chef-d'œuvre d’un bon harmoniste."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78bdf3f7-acdc-437a-aab5-3e3d4c76c287",
                                                "sense_id": "8ae988be-42fe-30a4-a474-ec7e974a18fb",
                                                "text": "La fugue est la pierre de touche du savoir des musiciens."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
